changeSet.sql:
COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.hook_failures.doc_id IS
  'No FK (RDR-194 D7): this column holds THREE identity spaces, discriminated by the sibling chain column. chain=''single'' stores a T3 chunk chash in hex (hook_registry.py _record_hook_failure). chain=''batch'' stores the FIRST chunk chash of the batch (hook_registry.py _record_batch_hook_failure: doc_ids[0] if doc_ids else the empty string; mcp_infra.py''s taxonomy_assign_batch tripwire persists the same shape). chain=''document'' stores a FILE PATH, never a tumbler and never a title (hook_registry.py _record_document_hook_failure: "Stores source_path in the legacy doc_id column"). The tumbler travels beside it as a separate catalog_doc_id kwarg on fire_batch/fire_document, never through this column. No single FK target exists for three referents and PostgreSQL has no conditional FK. Two further obstacles hold independently: the NOT NULL DEFAULT empty-string default can never satisfy an FK, and dropping it breaks idx_hook_failures_etl_dedup (tenant_id, doc_id, hook_name, occurred_at) since NULLs are distinct in a unique index. Occurrence-time remedy: if a dangling-doc_id population is ever observed on the telemetry read path, file then, with the count in hand. D8: the NOT NULL DEFAULT empty-string sentinel is ACCEPTED, not converted to NULL -- no FK attaches here, so no changeset exists to ride a conversion on.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.frecency.chunk_id IS
  'No FK, by GRAIN, not by deferral (RDR-194 D7). nexus.chunks is keyed (tenant_id, collection, chash); frecency has no collection column -- its PK is (tenant_id, chunk_id), one row per chash per tenant ACROSS collections by design. Adding a collection column to make an FK expressible would change the table''s identity grain, a behaviour change, not hygiene. The ChashCensus grain-mismatch leg for this table stays as the standing detection; D0.10''s one-for-one FK retirement does not fire here.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.relevance_log.chunk_id IS
  'No FK, by GRAIN, not by deferral (RDR-194 D7) -- the same reasoning as nexus.frecency.chunk_id: nexus.chunks is keyed (tenant_id, collection, chash) and relevance_log has no collection column, so an FK is not expressible without changing the table''s identity grain. The ChashCensus grain-mismatch leg for this table stays as the standing detection; D0.10''s one-for-one FK retirement does not fire here.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.pdf_chunks.chunk_id IS
  'No FK, same grain argument as nexus.frecency.chunk_id / nexus.relevance_log.chunk_id (RDR-194 D7). The pdf pipeline''s wire-parity rationale (pipeline-001-baseline.xml header) is already excluded from this RDR''s scope by the Problem Statement.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.chash_remap.old_id IS
  'Unconstrained TEXT by design (RDR-194 D3/D7): names a FOREIGN identity space -- "any pre-remap id" (RemapRepository.java) -- not a chash, so it has no plausible FK target. No FK from chash_remap to nexus.chunks either: a remap fact asserts a claim whose target may legitimately not be present yet, which is the exact measurement remap_membership performs (present_count vs mapped_total); an FK would make the function tautological. The sibling new_chash column''s own COMMENT (remap-003-new-chash-bytea.xml) named this column as the one whose reason lands in RDR-194 P4 -- this is that comment.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.gc_audit.id IS
  'BIGSERIAL PK, no natural key (RDR-194 D4): gc_audit is an append-only audit trail. A sequence hands out one value per row for the whole table, so PRIMARY KEY (id) already gives per-tenant uniqueness for free; promoting to (tenant_id, id) buys nothing while rewriting the PK index. RLS FORCE plus this sequence PK is the correct and sufficient tenant-isolation posture -- recorded here so it is not re-derived by a future census.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.claude_assisted_remediation_consents.id IS
  'BIGSERIAL PK, no natural key (RDR-194 D4): claude_assisted_remediation_consents is an append-only consent audit trail. A sequence hands out one value per row for the whole table, so PRIMARY KEY (id) already gives per-tenant uniqueness for free; promoting to (tenant_id, id) buys nothing while rewriting the PK index. RLS FORCE plus this sequence PK is the correct and sufficient tenant-isolation posture -- recorded here so it is not re-derived by a future census.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.gc_audit.collection IS
  'Empty-string sentinel ACCEPTED, not converted to NULL (RDR-194 D8): D7 attaches no FK to gc_audit.collection (a free-text label describing what was reaped, not a validated collection reference), so there is no FK changeset for a NULL conversion to ride.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.gc_audit.actor IS
  'Empty-string sentinel ACCEPTED, not converted to NULL (RDR-194 D8): D7 attaches no FK to gc_audit.actor (''engine'' for the server-driven producers wired at catalog-033, caller-supplied for client-attributed /gc_audit/record rows), so there is no FK changeset for a NULL conversion to ride.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.relevance_log.collection IS
  'Empty-string sentinel ACCEPTED, not converted to NULL (RDR-194 D8). No FK currently attaches to relevance_log.collection: D7 decided relevance_log.chunk_id (the grain argument) but left this sibling column''s own FK undecided, not deliberately loose. Named trigger: a future FK (tenant_id, collection) REFERENCES nexus.catalog_collections (tenant_id, name) on relevance_log.collection -- the same shape fk-002-collection-registry.xml and fk-004-chunks-collection-registry.xml already use for the collection registry -- is what would convert this sentinel to NULL, in that FK''s own changeset, never before it.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.relevance_log.session_id IS
  'Empty-string sentinel ACCEPTED, not converted to NULL (RDR-194 D8). relevance_log.session_id is a client session identifier, not a reference to any table in this schema -- there is no sessions table and none is planned, so unlike relevance_log.collection above, no FK is nameable as a future trigger for this column; the accepted position is permanent, not merely pending. idx_relevance_log_etl_dedup''s COALESCE(session_id, empty string) already treats the empty string and NULL as interchangeable for dedup purposes, so the sentinel is inert there regardless.';

rollback.sql:
COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.hook_failures.doc_id IS NULL;
COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.frecency.chunk_id IS NULL;
COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.relevance_log.chunk_id IS NULL;
COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.pdf_chunks.chunk_id IS NULL;
COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.chash_remap.old_id IS NULL;
COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.gc_audit.id IS NULL;
COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.claude_assisted_remediation_consents.id IS NULL;
COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.gc_audit.collection IS NULL;
COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.gc_audit.actor IS NULL;
COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.relevance_log.collection IS NULL;
COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.relevance_log.session_id IS NULL;
